      "content": "It's true that omeprazole can help reduce the risk of ulcers and some gastrointestinal issues, but it doesn't completely eliminate the risks associated with nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) like ibuprofen or Advil. These medications can still potentially cause irritation or ulcers, and omeprazole may not counteract all the possible side effects, especially with prolonged use. I'd strongly advise against using Advil without consulting with your healthcare provider. Managing both health concerns with professional guidance will likely result in a better outcome and could save you from potential complications down the road. If cost is an issue, please discuss it with your dentist or pharmacy—they may have options available to you.",
